      "content": "that makes sense. i want to make sure we're being as precise as possible though. when you mention \"minority populations\" and \"demographic volatility,\" how do those actually factor into the prediction math? \n\nlike, if we see a neighborhood with a high concentration of certain ethnic groups that has also seen a sudden shift in population density or socioeconomic status, does that increase the \"unrest\" score in the model? i'm trying to figure out if the model should weight those specific demographic shifts more heavily to preemptively identify where friction might happen.",
